# 15. DIRECTOR'S CUT MODE

Implement an advanced natural-language revision system called **DIRECTOR'S CUT**.

This feature allows users to revise an existing completed production through ordinary language.

The user should not need to manually locate every scene or repeat the original production prompt.

Example instructions:

"Make the entire film darker and more cinematic."

"Change the lighting in the second half."

"Make the main character's movements slower."

"Replace the final scene with a dramatic aerial shot."

"Add more rain throughout the production."

"Change the music to something more emotional."

"Make the camera movement smoother."

"Extend the opening scene by ten seconds."

"Use the new character reference in every scene."

"Make the environment match the new uploaded image."

The AI Director must interpret the requested change, identify affected scenes and assets, and determine the minimum necessary regeneration work.

## Intelligent Change Detection

Do not regenerate the entire film when only one scene needs modification.

Determine:

* Which scenes are affected.
* Which assets require modification.
* Which reference profiles must be updated.
* Whether audio needs adjustment.
* Whether scene timing changes.
* Whether downstream transitions need modification.

Preserve unaffected scenes.

## Version Control

Maintain production versions.

Allow users to:

* Save a new cut.
* Compare versions.
* Restore previous versions.
* Preview changes.
* View revision history.
* Identify modified scenes.
* Undo revisions.

Never overwrite the original production without preserving a recoverable version.

